  "summary": "A distinctive ceramic tradition known for its cobalt blue decorations on white earthenware.",
  "description": "Characterized by white clay vessels decorated with intricate cobalt blue geometric and floral patterns, often with a transparent lead glaze. This aesthetic developed in the coastal city of Safi, influenced by Islamic pottery traditions and maritime trade connections, producing functional and decorative items.",
